---
interface Props {
  agentId: string
  scope?: "global" | "project"
}

const { agentId, scope } = Astro.props
const command = [
  "npx",
  "--yes",
  "lyrashield@0.2.13",
  "install",
  agentId,
  scope ? `--${scope}` : null,
  "--dry-run",
]
  .filter(Boolean)
  .join(" ")
---

<h2>Preview the config entry with the published CLI</h2>
<p>
  <code>lyrashield@0.2.13</code> can preview the LyraShield server entry for this client. Keep{" "}
  <code>--dry-run</code>: config-writing installers are withheld while the safe-writer fix is pending
  release. The preview command changes no files.
</p>
<pre><code>{command}</code></pre>
<p>
  Manually merge only the LyraShield server entry into the documented configuration file below.
  Preserve existing servers and unrelated settings, retain comments where the format supports them,
  and edit the existing file through its current path without replacing a symlink or overwriting the
  whole file. Restart or reload the client and complete a read-only authenticated call; a config
  entry or CLI doctor result alone does not prove the client loaded the integration.
</p>
